{
  "category": "Rabbit Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "It slams foes by sharply uncoiling its rolled ears. It stings enough to make a grown-up cry in pain.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "When it senses danger, it perks up its ears. On cold nights, it sleeps with its head tucked into its fur.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its ears are always rolled up. They can be forcefully extended to shatter even a large boulder.",
      "version": "platinum"
    },
    {
      "text": "You can tell how it feels by the way it rolls its ears. When it’s scared, both ears are rolled up.",
      "version": "heartgold"
    },
    {
      "text": "You can tell how it feels by the way it rolls its ears. When it’s scared, both ears are rolled up.",
      "version": "soulsilver"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its ears are always rolled up. They can be forcefully extended to shatter even a large boulder.",
      "version": "black"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its ears are always rolled up. They can be forcefully extended to shatter even a large boulder.",
      "version": "white"
    },
    {
      "text": "By extending its rolled-up ears and striking the ground, it can bound so high it surprises itself.",
      "version": "black-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "By extending its rolled-up ears and striking the ground, it can bound so high it surprises itself.",
      "version": "white-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its ears are always rolled up. They can be forcefully extended to shatter even a large boulder.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "When it senses danger, it perks up its ears. On cold nights, it sleeps with its head tucked into its fur.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its ears are always rolled up. They can be forcefully extended to shatter even a large boulder.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "When it senses danger, it perks up its ears. On cold nights, it sleeps with its head tucked into its fur.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its arms and legs are weak, but when it rolls its ears up tight and then unleashes them with its full force, it can smash boulders to dust.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "The reason it keeps one ear rolled up is so it can launch a swift counterattack if it’s attacked by an enemy.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "If both of Buneary’s ears are rolled up, something is wrong with its body or mind. It’s a sure sign the Pokémon is in need of care.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "Buneary can attack by rolling up their ears and then striking with the force created by unrolling them. This attack becomes stronger with training.",
      "version": "shield"
    },
    {
      "text": "My hypothesis as to why Buneary rolls up its ears is that its hearing is far too keen. I surmise that the Pokémon protects its hearing by limiting the sound that may enter its ears.",
      "version": "legends-arceus"
    }
  ],
